Run:

az login

A browser window will open. Sign in to your Azure account.

Then verify the selected subscription:

az account show --output table

Don’t paste the subscription ID here. Just confirm that the correct subscription name appears.

After that, check Terraform:

terraform version

Then we’ll create the Azure Resource Group and ACR with Terraform.

Validate Terraform ISntalled or Install it:

winget install --exact --id Hashicorp.Terraform


Verify (reload Powershell):

terraform version

///////////////////////////////////////

Next, confirm Azure login without displaying your subscription ID:

az account show --query "{Name:name, State:state}" --output table

Then set the subscription ID only for the current PowerShell session:

$env:ARM_SUBSCRIPTION_ID = az account show --query id --output tsv

Do not put the subscription ID in Git.

Create this directory:

D:\GitHub\FastApiArgoProject\terraform

Inside it, create providers.tf:

terraform {
